1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Buying a resale ticket has always meant one question:

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,000
"Is this even real?"

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:14,000
FanPass answers that question before any money moves.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Here, a seller is uploading a FIFA World Cup ticket, straight from their phone.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The moment it lands, FanPass's AI Trust Engine takes over — six specialized agents working together.

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:32,000
One reads the ticket's QR code.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Another cross-checks the event, venue, and date against official fixtures.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
A third scans for signs of tampering or a reused screenshot.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Watch the Trust Score build in real time, climbing toward a hundred...

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
...each check lighting up green as it clears.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:01,000
This isn't a black box — every signal is shown, so a buyer can see exactly why a ticket is trusted.

12
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Once verified, the ticket becomes more than a listing — it becomes an on-chain Ownership Certificate.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:15,000
One signature from the seller's wallet, and it's live on the marketplace — priced, ranked, and ready.

14
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:19,000
Now, from the buyer's side.

15
00:01:19,000 --> 00:01:26,000
Here's the marketplace — every listing already carrying its Trust Score and seller reputation...

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:31,000
...sorted so the safest deals rise to the top.

17
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:38,000
This one — a Group Stage match at SoFi Stadium — eighty-four out of a hundred.

18
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:43,000
Fair price, verified seller, zero red flags.

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:48,000
The buyer connects their wallet, and taps Buy.

20
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:54,000
From here, FanPass never touches the money.

21
00:01:54,000 --> 00:02:01,000
The buyer's own wallet signs every step — approving the payment, locking funds in escrow on-chain...

22
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
...and finally releasing them to the seller.

23
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Three signatures. Full transparency. No middleman holding funds in between.

24
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:17,000
And just like that, the certificate transfers.

25
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
The ticket is now provably, verifiably theirs.

26
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:30,000
That's FanPass — turning ticket resale from a gamble... into a guarantee.
